Francesco D'Amato: So, whenever you change the Validator set, this reduces safety, because it reduces quorum intersection. So, once you exit them, this by itself reduces quorum intersection.

91
00:12:58.120 --> 00:13:10.280
Francesco D'Amato: And reuses safety. And this has nothing to do with even whether you keep… the stake can be frozen there, like, you can never let them exit, or never let them withdraw, but it still reuses safety.

92
00:13:10.280 --> 00:13:16.179
Francesco D'Amato: It's… it's not a question of the withdrawability delay in that case.

93
00:13:16.180 --> 00:13:27.010
Francesco D'Amato: It's just about the fact that you're reducing the quorum. So this is not something that we can fix. Basically, the only thing we can do there is that we don't fork until we have

94
