95
00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:51.890
Francesco D'Amato: 80% is fine, 90% is fine, like… I think, yeah, basically, like, anything that's sufficiently above 2 thirds, so that we still have some safety left, like, some slash stability left.

96
00:13:51.940 --> 00:14:01.589
Francesco D'Amato: That's for the non-PQ keys, then the bigger problem is the keys that are PQ, like, that exist on both sides of the fork.

97
00:14:01.590 --> 00:14:16.560
Francesco D'Amato: And for those is, like, their stake is still there, so there is no problem with the withdrawability delay, like, they're still part of the set, it's just that we probably will not have this automatic slashing across the fork, and so there, we still need to decide what to do.

98
00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:29.499
Francesco D'Amato: But, like, basically, we still need to be, you know, ready, potentially, to do some manual slashing. But we don't need to kind of force the state to stay there, because it's still part of the set, so it's there already.

