910
01:50:05.120 --> 01:50:12.319
Potuz: plus all of the single attestations that this node already has seen, the proposer has seen. The proposer is not so important as the attester.

911
01:50:13.130 --> 01:50:15.900
Justin Traglia: I thought the aggregate and proof topic was global.

912
01:50:16.410 --> 01:50:18.709
Justin Traglia: Like, why does the subnets matter?

913
01:50:19.690 --> 01:50:20.540
Potuz: I'm sorry?

914
01:50:21.530 --> 01:50:22.260
Justin Traglia: RM.

915
01:50:22.840 --> 01:50:24.219
Justin Traglia: Maybe I'm mistaken, I thought.

916
01:50:24.220 --> 01:50:38.010
Potuz: Oh, because the proposer needs to choose his head. So for the proposer, it's important that the attestation's reach before 2nd 12th. But for everyone else, it's important that these attestations are reached before 2nd 15.

917
01:50:38.130 --> 01:50:46.119
Potuz: So for everyone else, you have more broadcast time, but for the proposer, it's kind of critical that he knows the right head at second zero.

918
01:50:46.890 --> 01:50:55.990
Potuz: Therefore, the proposer will use the single attestation that its node already has, plus whatever aggregates he's gotten at second zero.

919
